{"task":"Let install run headless, and make doctor mode-aware","goals":"Install ldev in persite mode on this Mac without a sudo prompt, and have ldev doctor report the truth about a persite setup","status":"Completed","recorded_at":"2026-09-09T08:03:41Z","body":"confirm() returned success when nothing could answer it, so under `set -euo pipefail` a headless run either agreed to a sudo step nobody approved or died at the read. It now fails closed, and --skip-dns lets a run whose resolver and dnsmasq are already in place skip that step entirely instead of needing an answer for it.\n\ndoctor's end-to-end check only ever probed https://<TLD>/, which exists in auto mode alone: a healthy persite install reported a failure. It now walks each site's own Caddyfile. The host token is read only from real address lines — ones that are not comments and that end in the `{` opening a site block — because every generated Caddyfile also names its host in a header comment, and matching that comment first reported every site as portless, so all of them were probed on 443.\n","parent_commit":"476ad4b44be9afecbeaabb1ca92c8236a379ab27","repo":"ldev","pct":"100","tasks":[{"id":"install-persite","content":"Install ldev in persite mode on this Mac","status":"completed"},{"id":"confirm-fail-closed","content":"Make confirm() fail closed so a headless install cannot agree to sudo on the user's behalf","status":"completed"},{"id":"skip-dns","content":"Add --skip-dns so an install with resolver and dnsmasq already in place needs no sudo step","status":"completed"},{"id":"doctor-persite","content":"Make doctor's end-to-end check mode-aware instead of probing the auto-mode-only bare TLD","status":"completed"},{"id":"doctor-ports","content":"Read each host's port from real Caddyfile address lines, not from the header comment that names the same host","status":"completed"}],"agent":"claude-code","changelog":[{"text":"`bin/ldev` `cmd_doctor`: the end-to-end check now branches on `$MODE`. In `persite` it iterates `$SITES/*.$TLD/Caddyfile`, extracts each site's own host token from the address line (skipping comments, requiring a trailing `{`), defaults a portless host to 443, and curls `https://$host:$port/` per site; prints a note when no per-site Caddyfiles exist. `auto`/`apache` keep the old single `https://$TLD/` probe.","kind":"info","priority":"low","state":"complete","explicit":false,"tags":["error-handling"]},{"text":"`install.sh` `confirm()`: non-tty now returns 1 (decline) instead of 0 (accept). Unattended runs no longer auto-approve sudo steps that would then die under `set -e`; `--yes`/`--defaults` still mean yes.","kind":"info","priority":"low","state":"complete","explicit":false,"tags":["error-handling"]},{"text":"`install.sh`: new `--skip-dns` flag (parsed, documented in the header usage block picked up by `--help`) that skips the `/etc/resolver` + dnsmasq step entirely.","kind":"info","priority":"low","state":"complete","explicit":false,"tags":["build-config"]},{"text":"`install.sh`: the resolver step is also skipped when `/etc/resolver/$TLD` exists **and** `dnsmasq` is running, avoiding a redundant sudo prompt.","kind":"info","priority":"low","state":"complete","explicit":false,"tags":["build-config"]}],"code_quality":[{"text":"`bin/ldev` — the per-site branch ends with `[ \"$found\" = 0 ] && note \"no per-site Caddyfiles yet …\"`. If `bin/ldev` runs under `set -e`, this line returns 1 whenever sites *were* found, aborting `cmd_doctor` before the final pass/fail summary. Verify whether `set -e` is set; if so, rewrite as `if [ \"$found\" = 0 ]; then note …; fi`.","kind":"task","priority":"low","state":"needs_review","effort":"quick","tags":["error-handling"]},{"text":"`install.sh` — the `elif` only checks that the resolver file exists, not that its contents point at dnsmasq; a stale/wrong `/etc/resolver/$TLD` is now silently accepted.","kind":"info","priority":"low","state":"needs_review","tags":["error-handling"]}],"vulnerabilities":[{"text":"`bin/ldev` (per-site probe) — the new call uses `curl -sk`, while the auto-mode probe kept plain `curl -s`. `-k` disables TLS verification, so doctor reports `200` for a site whose certificate is expired, untrusted, or not in the keychain — which is precisely the failure this tool exists to detect, and it silently diverges from what auto mode validates. Drop `-k` (or, if per-site certs genuinely aren't in the trust store, verify explicitly against the local CA rather than skipping verification) and keep both branches consistent.","kind":"task","priority":"low","state":"complete","resolved_by":"7b6b394f2967389fef8998f5cfa92cf228bf7d35","tags":["security"],"history":[{"at":"2026-09-09T08:06:34.153Z","type":"resolved","by":"claude:84a94ca3-be6f-45bb-bfed-90e7f8bab9ad","commit":"7b6b394f2967389fef8998f5cfa92cf228bf7d35"}]},{"text":"No other security concerns: no secrets, no injection into a shell (`$host`/`$port` come from directory/Caddyfile names and are only interpolated into a curl URL argument, not `eval`'d), and the privilege change is strictly more conservative.","kind":"info","priority":"low","state":"complete","explicit":false}],"code_style_suggestions":[{"text":"`install.sh` — the body under the new `else` (from `say \"Next step needs sudo…\"` through the closing `fi`) is left at the original indentation, so the nested block reads as top-level. Indent it two spaces to match.","kind":"task","priority":"low","state":"complete","effort":"quick","resolved_by":"7b6b394f2967389fef8998f5cfa92cf228bf7d35","tags":["readability"],"history":[{"at":"2026-09-09T08:06:39.984Z","type":"resolved","by":"claude:84a94ca3-be6f-45bb-bfed-90e7f8bab9ad","commit":"7b6b394f2967389fef8998f5cfa92cf228bf7d35"}]},{"text":"`$host` is interpolated into an ERE where its dots match any character; harmless here, but `${host//./\\\\.}` would be exact.","kind":"info","priority":"low","state":"needs_review","tags":["readability"]}],"reusability":[{"text":"The three-way `200`/`000`/other reporting is now duplicated in both branches; a small `probe_url <url>` helper would collapse it.","kind":"info","priority":"low","state":"needs_review","tags":["duplication"]}],"system_compatibility":[{"text":"`confirm()` returning 1 on a non-tty is an intentional behaviour break for any existing CI/piped install that relied on implicit yes without `--yes`; those invocations now silently skip the DNS/cert steps.","kind":"info","priority":"low","state":"needs_review","tags":["compatibility"]}],"review_run":{"state":"ran","at":"2026-09-09T08:03:40Z","attempts":1,"agent":"claude","mode":"light"}}
